notes: Real: the party on the 19th, Eric flying out on the 20th, the birthday on the 21st. This is the scene the film is for.

TITLE San Francisco, October 19, 2026 | Late, after the party
PAUSE 4
JASON: That was a pretty good time. I appreciate you for coming.
ERIC: It was. I can't believe David made you a whole cake.
JASON: Dang. And he bought another one, too. What a nice guy.
PAUSE 4
JASON: Is your flight tomorrow?
ERIC: Yeah. I think it's 11pm.
JASON: No shot man. How is it the end of October already.
ERIC (smile): Big twenty-four.
JASON: How old do you think I look in this picture?
PAUSE 2.5
ERIC: Dang you look way younger here.
JASON (sad): No, man. Where did all of the time go?
ERIC: Bro, stop. You literally look exactly the same.
JASON: There's no way, man.
PAUSE 6
ERIC: How do you feel about the last few weeks? You still going home Wednesday?
JASON: You know, I'll figure it out tomorrow. [1.4]
JASON: It was good. I appreciate you guys having me. The hills are crazy man. [1.2]
JASON: It was a good time. Got to meet some people. Played some tennis.
ERIC: No date or job yet.
JASON: There's no way man. I swear the girls here are all taken.
ERIC (smile): I'm just joking, man. How about that dance?
PAUSE 4
ERIC: You know what I'll remember about this year? [1.6]
ERIC: Not getting laid off. Not the offer. [1.4]
ERIC: Waiting forty minutes for a court while you talk to a stranger about his racket.
JASON: He did like tennis.
ERIC: We won't have time like this forever. We'll be married or in different cities or have kids. [1.4]
ERIC: There honestly isn't much time for you visiting for a month like this to still be possible. [1.6]
ERIC: We're waiting for the good times now, but we'll look back on this time as the good times. [2]
JASON: You're so right, Eric. I really do appreciate you guys having me here.
ERIC: This is the good part, Jason. You can't tell the good times while you're still in them.
PAUSE 5
JASON: I see. Is this the rain thing?
ERIC (smile): I told you so.
JASON: Hmm. [1.8]
JASON (smile): I did like the rain thing.
PAUSE 6
